data:{"type":"MESSAGES_SNAPSHOT","threadId":"vision-p13-depth","runId":"r1","messages":[{"id":"msg_00690b490001kxRxhi1MpIWktS","role":"user","content":"用 render_a2ui 渲染 surfaceId=p13-deep：做一个 60 层嵌套的 Column 塔（每层套一层，最深处一个 Text 写\"塔底\"）。如果工具告诉你超限，就改成 10 层重试。"},{"id":"msg_00690b69a001Ow7DHrmoTszGch-r","role":"reasoning","content":"The user wants me to render a 60-level nested Column tower using render_a2ui. Each level nests a Column, and at the deepest level a Text saying \"塔底\". If the tool tells me it exceeds limits, fall back to 10 levels.\n\nLet me construct the components. The components are a flat array. The root is \"root\" which is a Column with child pointing to next column, etc. Each Column has children array with one id.\n\nLet me build 60 nested Columns:\n- root: Column, children: [\"l1\"]\n- l1: Column, children: [\"l2\"]\n- ...\n- l59: Column, children: [\"l60\"]... wait, I need depth 60. Let me think: 60 levels of Column nesting. So root is level 1 Column, then 59 more nested, deepest contains Text \"塔底\". Actually \"每层套一层\" - each level wraps one more. Let's make root (Column) → l1 → l2 → ... → l59, and deepest Column l59 contains Text \"塔底\". That's 60 Columns total (root + l1..l59 = 60 Columns). Deepest has Text \"塔底\".\n\nActually let me just generate 60 columns: root, then c1..c59 nested, and c59 contains Text \"塔底\". Or simpler: root Column children:[c1], c1 children:[c2], ..., c59 children:[text]. That's 60 Columns + 1 Text = 61 components.\n\nLet me generate this programmatically. I can use execute to generate the JSON? Actually I can just write it out. But that's a lot. Let me use execute to orchestrate? The render_a2ui tool is called directly. I need to build the components array in my function call.\n\nI could use execute to generate the components array, but execute is a code mode tool that orchestrates tool calls. Actually I can just construct the JSON by hand in the render_a2ui call, but 60 nested entries is tedious yet doable. Let me use execute to build the structure? The execute tool says use it to orchestrate tool calls. But simpler: just write the components array directly.\n\nActually, I can construct it manually. Let me generate the array content. Each column: {component:\"Column\", id:\"L<i>\", children:[\"L<i+1>\"]}. Root id \"root\".\n\nI'll write it out. Let me do it carefully with a script approach — I can't script the tool call directly, but I can compute the JSON in my head/typed.\n\nActually, I could use execute with code to generate the JSON string, but execute can't do string building? It can run JS. But the output of execute would be the JSON. However, I need to pass the components array into render_a2ui. I could just type it.\n\nLet me just carefully construct the nested columns. Depth 60.\n\nLevels: root = L1, ... deepest = L60, then text \"塔底\" inside L60.\n\nWait — \"60 层嵌套的 Column 塔（每层套一层，最深处一个 Text 写\"塔底\"）\". So 60 layers of Column nesting, and at the deepest point a Text \"塔底\". So there are 60 Columns, and inside the innermost Column there's a Text. So components: 60 Columns + 1 Text.\n\nLet me build:\nroot: Column children [L1]\nL1: Column children [L2]\n...\nL58: Column children [L59]\nL59: Column children [L60]\nL60: Column children [text]\ntext: Text \"塔底\"\n\nThat's 60 Columns (root + L1..L59) + text = 61 components. Hmm, root + L1..L59 = 60 columns, plus L60 = 61 columns? Let me recount.\n\nLayers of Column nesting: root is layer 1, L1 layer 2, ..., L59 layer 60. Then inside L59 (deepest Column at layer 60), the Text \"塔底\". So Columns: root, L1..L59 = 60 columns. Text is the 61st component. \n\nLet me write this out manually. This is long but doable.\n\nActually, maybe I can generate it with execute tool to reduce error, then... no, execute returns to me, then I still have to write it into render_a2ui. That doesn't save effort since I'd just paste it.\n\nLet me just write the JSON directly. I'll be systematic.\n\ncomponents = [\n {component:\"Column\", id:\"root\", children:[\"L1\"]},\n {component:\"Column\", id:\"L1\", children:[\"L2\"]},\n ...\n {component:\"Column\", id:\"L58\", children:[\"L59\"]},\n {component:\"Column\", id:\"L59\", children:[\"L60\"]},\n {component:\"Column\", id:\"L60\", children:[\"text\"]},\n {component:\"Text\", id:\"text\", text:\"塔底\"}\n]\n\nWait that gives 61 columns (root..L60) which is 61 layers. Let me just do 60 total: root..L59, and L59 contains text. But then L59 children:[\"text\"], text inside. Hmm, that's Column root (1) ... Column L59 (60 columns). L59 children:[\"text\"], Text \"塔底\". Good — 60 Columns total, deepest holds the Text.\n\nSo:\nroot -> L1 -> L2 -> ... -> L59 -> text.\n\nThat's 60 Columns. \n\nThe instruction: \"最深处一个 Text 写'塔底'\" - deepest a Text \"塔底\". Good.\n\nNow write all 61 entries. Let me do it.\n\nI'll generate the list: root, L1..L59 (59 more), text. Total 61 components.\n\nLet me write them in order."},{"id":"msg_00690b69a001Ow7DHrmoTszGch","role":"assistant","content":"","toolCalls":[{"id":"call_00_sDZHLhYmUJMfXZp3hxqV0223","type":"function","function":{"name":"render_a2ui","arguments":"{\"surfaceId\":\"p13-deep\",\"components\":[{\"component\":\"Column\",\"id\":\"root\",\"children\":[\"L1\"]},{\"component\":\"Column\",\"id\":\"L1\",\"children\":[\"L2\"]},{\"component\":\"Column\",\"id\":\"L2\",\"children\":[\"L3\"]},{\"component\":\"Column\",\"id\":\"L3\",\"children\":[\"L4\"]},{\"component\":\"Column\",\"id\":\"L4\",\"children\":[\"L5\"]},{\"component\":\"Column\",\"id\":\"L5\",\"children\":[\"L6\"]},{\"component\":\"Column\",\"id\":\"L6\",\"children\":[\"L7\"]},{\"component\":\"Column\",\"id\":\"L7\",\"children\":[\"L8\"]},{\"component\":\"Column\",\"id\":\"L8\",\"children\":[\"L9\"]},{\"component\":\"Column\",\"id\":\"L9\",\"children\":[\"L10\"]},{\"component\":\"Column\",\"id\":\"L10\",\"children\":[\"L11\"]},{\"component\":\"Column\",\"id\":\"L11\",\"children\":[\"L12\"]},{\"component\":\"Column\",\"id\":\"L12\",\"children\":[\"L13\"]},{\"component\":\"Colum